-- SECTION A JOIN: Decree 67/2023 (VN-10, the `nd67-*` modules) to Law 08/2022/QH15 (VN-29, the `law08-*` modules).
-- The relation is "this decree field instantiates this Law status", not a shared type. Each function below builds a
-- record of VN-29 (a record of witness facts) from records of VN-10, and each assertion asks the Law's own predicate
-- of the record built. SECTION-A.md holds the table these functions check; its row ids (A01 ...) label the blocks here.
-- Citations are `decree67:N` (line N of reference/decree67.txt) and `law08:N` (line N of reference/law08.txt).
-- Assertions are anonymous in L4, so each carries a label in a comment, [A03.2] and so on; SECTION-A.md cites those labels.
--
-- TWO ASSUMPTIONS MADE FOR THE WHOLE FILE (assumed, not ruled):
--  1. A fact the decree does not state is supplied by the caller or defaults to FALSE; the join never invents a fact
--     that would make a Law predicate hold. Where the decree supplies the fact only by implication, the comment says so.
--  2. Law vintages: V1 is pinned at 2025-06-01, V2 at 2026-03-01 and V3 at 2026-08-01, as VN-29's own tests pin them.
--     A Law predicate with no vintage arm in VN-29 gives one answer in all three; the standard-case assertion of each row
--     is run in all three to show it, rather than assumed.
--
-- NAME COLLISIONS. The only name VN-10 and VN-29 both declare is the constructor `the insurer` (VN-10: A party to the
-- claim; VN-29: A party to the contract). The module-qualified spelling the brief prescribes (module name, a dot, the
-- name) is refused by this `l4` build for every spelling tried (see SECTION-A.md section 0), so each use below sits where
-- the expected type picks the constructor, and two typed aliases name them apart: `the decree's insurer`, `the Law's insurer`.

§ `Section A join`

§§ `Names for the two vintages, and the typed aliases`

`the decree as made` MEANS `Decree 67/2023 as made`
`the decree as amended` MEANS `Decree 67/2023 as amended by Decree 220/2026`

GIVETH A `A party to the claim`
`the decree's insurer` MEANS `the insurer`

GIVETH A `A party to the contract`
`the Law's insurer` MEANS `the insurer`

-- Two parts of one cover. VN-10 has Article 4(3)'s split only as two Booleans; the Law's Dieu 8 and 87 ask which part
-- a product is, so the join names the two parts.
DECLARE `A part of the cover` IS ONE OF
    `the part the decree requires`
    `an extension the parties agreed under Article 4(3)`

-- Article 6 sets two limits of different shape (decree67:187-196): per person per accident for health and life, per accident
-- for property, by the class of the vehicle.
DECLARE `A harm a limit of Article 6 applies to` IS ONE OF
    `harm to the health or life of one person`
    `damage to property in one accident` HAS `the class of the vehicle` IS A `A vehicle class in Annex I`

GIVEN r IS AN EITHER `A problem with the facts` NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the decree finds a problem in` r MEANS
    CONSIDER r
    WHEN LEFT problem THEN TRUE
    WHEN RIGHT amount THEN FALSE

GIVEN r IS AN EITHER `A problem with the facts` BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the decree answers yes in` r MEANS
    CONSIDER r
    WHEN LEFT problem THEN FALSE
    WHEN RIGHT answer THEN answer

§§ `Fixtures: the decree's standard case and its carve-outs`

-- Vehicles. A private car of 5 seats needs a driving licence; the second is past its service life (decree67:125-128,
-- Article 4(5)(a)); the third is a two-wheeled motorcycle of 150 cc.
`a private car` MEANS `A motor vehicle` WITH
    `class in Annex I` IS `a car not used for transport business` 5
    `beyond its service life under the law` IS FALSE
    `a foreign vehicle temporarily imported for re-export, in traffic in Vietnam for less than 1 year` IS FALSE
    `remaining service life under the law of less than 1 year` IS FALSE
    `subject to temporary registration` IS FALSE
    `a driving licence is required to drive it` IS TRUE

`a private car past its service life` MEANS `A motor vehicle` WITH
    `class in Annex I` IS `a car not used for transport business` 5
    `beyond its service life under the law` IS TRUE
    `a foreign vehicle temporarily imported for re-export, in traffic in Vietnam for less than 1 year` IS FALSE
    `remaining service life under the law of less than 1 year` IS FALSE
    `subject to temporary registration` IS FALSE
    `a driving licence is required to drive it` IS TRUE

`a motorcycle of 150 cc` MEANS `A motor vehicle` WITH
    `class in Annex I` IS `a two-wheeled motorcycle` 150
    `beyond its service life under the law` IS FALSE
    `a foreign vehicle temporarily imported for re-export, in traffic in Vietnam for less than 1 year` IS FALSE
    `remaining service life under the law of less than 1 year` IS FALSE
    `subject to temporary registration` IS FALSE
    `a driving licence is required to drive it` IS TRUE

-- Contracts. The premium for a private car of 5 seats for one year is the Annex I figure 437,000 (A.IV.1).
