    `operates to carry on insurance brokerage activity` IS FALSE
    `carries on life insurance` IS FALSE
    `carries on non-life insurance` IS FALSE
    `carries on health insurance` IS FALSE
    `is a legal person` IS FALSE
    `is a dependent unit of a foreign insurer or reinsurer` IS TRUE
    `the foreign insurer or reinsurer guarantees and answers for all its obligations in Vietnam` IS TRUE
    `keeps independent accounts` IS FALSE
    `was founded by members or a body representing members` IS FALSE
    `operates without a profit purpose, for mutual support among members` IS FALSE
    `is voluntary, financially autonomous and answerable only within the assets formed from microinsurance` IS FALSE
    `the foreign body is a non-life insurer` IS TRUE
    `the foreign body is a reinsurer` IS FALSE

§§ `A01 and A02: the policyholder and the insured person (Dieu 4(24), 4(25))`

-- Decree: the buyer is the owner who must buy (Art 4(1), decree67:103-106); the insured liability is the owner's (Art 5,
-- decree67:183-186). VN-10 keeps the buyer and the insured in ONE constructor, `the insurance buyer or the insured`, and
-- the owner in another; the Law keeps the two statuses apart (law08:167-172). A role record bundles the facts about one person,
-- so one record answers both statuses.
GIVEN c IS A `A contract of compulsory motor insurance`
GIVETH A `A role in a contract`
`the role of the owner who bought the cover, on the facts of` c MEANS
    `A role in a contract` WITH
        `concluded the contract of insurance with an insurer, branch or mutual organisation` IS TRUE
        `pays the insurance premium` IS c's `the premium paid` GREATER THAN 0
        `has property, civil liability, health, life, an obligation or an economic interest insured under the contract` IS TRUE
        `was designated by the policyholder or the insured person to receive the insurance money as the contract agrees` IS FALSE

-- A01. The Law's role of a party the decree names. The insurer is the other side of the contract and the injured person is
-- neither side of it (decree67:344-349 pays that person, but names no designation).
GIVEN party IS A `A party to the claim`
      c     IS A `A contract of compulsory motor insurance`
GIVETH A `A role in a contract`
`the Law's role for the decree's insurance buyer` party c MEANS
    CONSIDER party
    WHEN `the insurer`                        THEN `a person with no role in the contract`
    WHEN `the insurance buyer or the insured` THEN `the role of the owner who bought the cover, on the facts of` c
    WHEN `the injured person`                 THEN `a person with no role in the contract`
    WHEN `the vehicle owner`                  THEN `the role of the owner who bought the cover, on the facts of` c

-- A02. The insured person: VN-10 merges the two statuses, so the same record answers Dieu 4(25).
GIVEN party IS A `A party to the claim`
      c     IS A `A contract of compulsory motor insurance`
GIVETH A `A role in a contract`
`the Law's role for the decree's insured` party c MEANS
    `the Law's role for the decree's insurance buyer` party c

-- [A01.1] The decree's buyer-or-insured, with the premium paid, is the Law's policyholder; so is the owner.
#ASSERT `Dieu 4(24): the person is the policyholder (ben mua bao hiem)` (`the Law's role for the decree's insurance buyer` `the insurance buyer or the insured` `a contract concluded in 2024`)
#ASSERT `Dieu 4(24): the person is the policyholder (ben mua bao hiem)` (`the Law's role for the decree's insurance buyer` `the vehicle owner` `a contract concluded in 2024`)
-- [A01.2] Carve-outs: the insurer is the other party, the injured person is neither; an owner who has paid nothing
-- (the decree makes the owner BUY, Art 4(1); the Law's status needs the premium paid) is not yet one.
#ASSERT NOT `Dieu 4(24): the person is the policyholder (ben mua bao hiem)` (`the Law's role for the decree's insurance buyer` `the decree's insurer` `a contract concluded in 2024`)
#ASSERT NOT `Dieu 4(24): the person is the policyholder (ben mua bao hiem)` (`the Law's role for the decree's insurance buyer` `the injured person` `a contract concluded in 2024`)
#ASSERT NOT `Dieu 4(24): the person is the policyholder (ben mua bao hiem)` (`the Law's role for the decree's insurance buyer` `the insurance buyer or the insured` `a contract of 2024 on which no premium was paid`)
-- [A01.3] Dieu 4 has no vintage arm in VN-29: the standard case in V1, V2 and V3.
#ASSERT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (YMD 2025 6 1) (`Dieu 4(24): the person is the policyholder (ben mua bao hiem)` (`the Law's role for the decree's insurance buyer` `the insurance buyer or the insured` `a contract concluded in 2024`))
#ASSERT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (YMD 2026 3 1) (`Dieu 4(24): the person is the policyholder (ben mua bao hiem)` (`the Law's role for the decree's insurance buyer` `the insurance buyer or the insured` `a contract concluded in 2024`))
#ASSERT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (YMD 2026 8 1) (`Dieu 4(24): the person is the policyholder (ben mua bao hiem)` (`the Law's role for the decree's insurance buyer` `the insurance buyer or the insured` `a contract concluded in 2024`))

-- [A02.1] The merged party is also the Law's insured person; so is the owner (Art 5).
#ASSERT `Dieu 4(25): the person is the insured person (nguoi duoc bao hiem)` (`the Law's role for the decree's insured` `the insurance buyer or the insured` `a contract concluded in 2024`)
#ASSERT `Dieu 4(25): the person is the insured person (nguoi duoc bao hiem)` (`the Law's role for the decree's insured` `the vehicle owner` `a contract concluded in 2024`)
-- [A02.2] Neither the insurer nor the injured person is insured under the contract.
#ASSERT NOT `Dieu 4(25): the person is the insured person (nguoi duoc bao hiem)` (`the Law's role for the decree's insured` `the decree's insurer` `a contract concluded in 2024`)
#ASSERT NOT `Dieu 4(25): the person is the insured person (nguoi duoc bao hiem)` (`the Law's role for the decree's insured` `the injured person` `a contract concluded in 2024`)
-- [A02.3] The merge: ONE decree party is both of two statuses the Law keeps apart; and an owner whose premium is unpaid is
-- still the insured person but not yet the policyholder.
#ASSERT `Dieu 4(24): the person is the policyholder (ben mua bao hiem)` (`the Law's role for the decree's insurance buyer` `the insurance buyer or the insured` `a contract concluded in 2024`) AND `Dieu 4(25): the person is the insured person (nguoi duoc bao hiem)` (`the Law's role for the decree's insured` `the insurance buyer or the insured` `a contract concluded in 2024`)
#ASSERT `Dieu 4(25): the person is the insured person (nguoi duoc bao hiem)` (`the Law's role for the decree's insured` `the insurance buyer or the insured` `a contract of 2024 on which no premium was paid`) AND NOT `Dieu 4(24): the person is the policyholder (ben mua bao hiem)` (`the Law's role for the decree's insurance buyer` `the insurance buyer or the insured` `a contract of 2024 on which no premium was paid`)
-- [A02.4] Dieu 4(25) in V1, V2 and V3.
#ASSERT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (YMD 2025 6 1) (`Dieu 4(25): the person is the insured person (nguoi duoc bao hiem)` (`the Law's role for the decree's insured` `the insurance buyer or the insured` `a contract concluded in 2024`))
#ASSERT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (YMD 2026 3 1) (`Dieu 4(25): the person is the insured person (nguoi duoc bao hiem)` (`the Law's role for the decree's insured` `the insurance buyer or the insured` `a contract concluded in 2024`))
#ASSERT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (YMD 2026 8 1) (`Dieu 4(25): the person is the insured person (nguoi duoc bao hiem)` (`the Law's role for the decree's insured` `the insurance buyer or the insured` `a contract concluded in 2024`))

§§ `A03, A04 and A16: the third person (the Law's use of it, Dieu 4(14), 30(3), 57-61)`

-- The Law uses "third person" (law08:128-129, 715-717, 1076-1124) and never defines it. The decree defines it for this
-- insurance with four exceptions (Art 3(5)(a), decree67:84-89). VN-29 has no record of a third person; the nearest
-- is the liability claim of Dieu 58-59, whose first fact is that a third person claimed from the insured person. So the join
-- builds that claim and lets the DECREE say who counts as the third person.
-- The Law's Dieu 58(2) bars a direct claim "unless the law provides otherwise": Art 12(5) second paragraph (decree67:344-349)
-- pays the injured person directly when the insured has died or lost civil capacity, and only then.
GIVEN `the harmed person counts as a third person` IS A BOOLEAN
      a      IS AN `An accident`
      c      IS A `A contract of compulsory motor insurance`
      gone   IS A BOOLEAN
      claimed IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `A liability contract and a claim`
`the Law's liability claim, once the decree has said who the third person is` `the harmed person counts as a third person` a c gone claimed MEANS
    `A liability contract and a claim` WITH
        `a third person claimed compensation from the insured person` IS `the harmed person counts as a third person` AND claimed
        `the act causing the damage occurred within the insurance term` IS c's `insurance begins on` AT MOST a's `date of the accident` AND a's `date of the accident` AT MOST c's `insurance ends on`
        `the third person's claim was made within the insurance term` IS FALSE
        `the third person claims directly from the insurer` IS gone AND `the harmed person counts as a third person` AND claimed
        `the law provides that the third person may claim directly` IS gone AND `the harmed person counts as a third person`
        `amount the insured person must pay the third person by law` IS 0
        `costs of resolving the dispute on liability to the third person` IS 0
        `interest payable to the third person for the insured person's late payment as the insurer directed` IS 0
        `limit of liability` IS 0
        `the contract agrees otherwise on the limit` IS FALSE
        `the insured person must post a bond or deposit to keep the property from detention or to avoid a suit` IS FALSE
        `the insured person asks the insurer to give the bond or deposit` IS FALSE
        `the contract so agrees` IS FALSE
        `the insurer negotiates with the third person for the insured person` IS FALSE
        `the contract agrees otherwise on representation` IS FALSE

-- A03. The third person is the decree's third party (Article 3(5)(a)), in the vintage given.
GIVEN v       IS A `A vintage of Decree 67/2023`
      p       IS A `A person harmed in the accident`
      a       IS AN `An accident`
      c       IS A `A contract of compulsory motor insurance`
      gone    IS A BOOLEAN
      claimed IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `A liability contract and a claim`
`the Law's liability claim of the decree's third party` v p a c gone claimed MEANS
    `the Law's liability claim, once the decree has said who the third person is` (`Article 3(5)(a) — a third party` v p a) a c gone claimed

-- A04. The same, but the vintage is the one that governs the contract (Art 76(1); Decree 220 Art 10); a contract that
-- Art 76(1) leaves under earlier rules is refused, as VN-10 refuses it.
GIVEN c       IS A `A contract of compulsory motor insurance`
      p       IS A `A person harmed in the accident`
      a       IS AN `An accident`
      gone    IS A BOOLEAN
      claimed IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `A liability contract and a claim`
`the Law's liability claim of the third party under the contract` c p a gone claimed MEANS
    `the Law's liability claim of the decree's third party` (`the vintage that governs` c) p a c gone claimed

-- A16. The third person is anyone to whom Art 5 says the owner's liability is owed: the third party AND the passengers
-- (decree67:183-186; the object of the insurance, which Dieu 57 fixes as liability to a third person, law08:1076-1078).
GIVEN v       IS A `A vintage of Decree 67/2023`
      p       IS A `A person harmed in the accident`
      a       IS AN `An accident`
      c       IS A `A contract of compulsory motor insurance`
      gone    IS A BOOLEAN
      claimed IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `A liability contract and a claim`
`the Law's liability claim of a person the owner's insured liability is owed to` v p a c gone claimed MEANS
    `the Law's liability claim, once the decree has said who the third person is` (`Article 5 — the owner's insured liability is owed to` v p a) a c gone claimed

-- [A03.1] The standard case, decree as made: the third party's claim, in the term, engages the insurer (Dieu 58(1)).
#ASSERT `Dieu 58(1): the insurer's liability arises` (`the Law's liability claim of the decree's third party` `the decree as made` `a third party who was harmed` `the standard accident` `a contract concluded in 2024` FALSE TRUE)
-- [A03.2] Carve-outs, decree as made: the driver, a person on the vehicle, a passenger, and the owner who has not handed
-- the car to another are not third parties, so no third person's claim exists and Dieu 58(1) is not engaged.
#ASSERT NOT `Dieu 58(1): the insurer's liability arises` (`the Law's liability claim of the decree's third party` `the decree as made` `the driver who was harmed` `the standard accident` `a contract concluded in 2024` FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `Dieu 58(1): the insurer's liability arises` (`the Law's liability claim of the decree's third party` `the decree as made` `a person on the vehicle who was harmed` `the standard accident` `a contract concluded in 2024` FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `Dieu 58(1): the insurer's liability arises` (`the Law's liability claim of the decree's third party` `the decree as made` `a passenger on the vehicle who was harmed` `the standard accident` `a contract concluded in 2024` FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `Dieu 58(1): the insurer's liability arises` (`the Law's liability claim of the decree's third party` `the decree as made` `the owner of the vehicle who was harmed` `the standard accident` `a contract concluded in 2024` FALSE TRUE)
-- [A03.3] ... save the owner who has handed the vehicle to another, who is a third party.
#ASSERT `Dieu 58(1): the insurer's liability arises` (`the Law's liability claim of the decree's third party` `the decree as made` `the owner of the vehicle who was harmed` `an accident in which the owner had handed the car to another` `a contract concluded in 2024` FALSE TRUE)
-- [A03.4] The same six results, decree as amended by Decree 220/2026 (the word changes, the persons do not).
#ASSERT `Dieu 58(1): the insurer's liability arises` (`the Law's liability claim of the decree's third party` `the decree as amended` `a third party who was harmed` `the standard accident` `a contract concluded in 2024` FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `Dieu 58(1): the insurer's liability arises` (`the Law's liability claim of the decree's third party` `the decree as amended` `the driver who was harmed` `the standard accident` `a contract concluded in 2024` FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `Dieu 58(1): the insurer's liability arises` (`the Law's liability claim of the decree's third party` `the decree as amended` `a person on the vehicle who was harmed` `the standard accident` `a contract concluded in 2024` FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `Dieu 58(1): the insurer's liability arises` (`the Law's liability claim of the decree's third party` `the decree as amended` `a passenger on the vehicle who was harmed` `the standard accident` `a contract concluded in 2024` FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `Dieu 58(1): the insurer's liability arises` (`the Law's liability claim of the decree's third party` `the decree as amended` `the owner of the vehicle who was harmed` `the standard accident` `a contract concluded in 2024` FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT `Dieu 58(1): the insurer's liability arises` (`the Law's liability claim of the decree's third party` `the decree as amended` `the owner of the vehicle who was harmed` `an accident in which the owner had handed the car to another` `a contract concluded in 2024` FALSE TRUE)
-- [A03.5] Control: the act outside the insurance term engages nothing, third party or not (Dieu 58(1), occurrence reading).
#ASSERT NOT `Dieu 58(1): the insurer's liability arises` (`the Law's liability claim of the decree's third party` `the decree as made` `a third party who was harmed` `an accident after the insurance had ended` `a contract concluded in 2024` FALSE TRUE)
-- [A03.6] No direct claim on the insurer (Dieu 58(2)) while the insured is alive; one when the insured has died or lost civil
-- capacity (Art 12(5), second paragraph) -- but only for a person who is a third party.
#ASSERT NOT `Dieu 58(2): the third person may claim directly from the insurer` (`the Law's liability claim of the decree's third party` `the decree as made` `a third party who was harmed` `the standard accident` `a contract concluded in 2024` FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT `Dieu 58(2): the third person may claim directly from the insurer` (`the Law's liability claim of the decree's third party` `the decree as made` `a third party who was harmed` `the standard accident` `a contract concluded in 2024` TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `Dieu 58(2): the third person may claim directly from the insurer` (`the Law's liability claim of the decree's third party` `the decree as made` `the driver who was harmed` `the standard accident` `a contract concluded in 2024` TRUE TRUE)
-- [A03.7] Dieu 58(1) in V1, V2 and V3.
#ASSERT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (YMD 2025 6 1) (`Dieu 58(1): the insurer's liability arises` (`the Law's liability claim of the decree's third party` `the decree as made` `a third party who was harmed` `the standard accident` `a contract concluded in 2024` FALSE TRUE))
#ASSERT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (YMD 2026 3 1) (`Dieu 58(1): the insurer's liability arises` (`the Law's liability claim of the decree's third party` `the decree as made` `a third party who was harmed` `the standard accident` `a contract concluded in 2024` FALSE TRUE))
#ASSERT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (YMD 2026 8 1) (`Dieu 58(1): the insurer's liability arises` (`the Law's liability claim of the decree's third party` `the decree as made` `a third party who was harmed` `the standard accident` `a contract concluded in 2024` FALSE TRUE))

-- [A04.1] The vintage comes from the contract: concluded in August 2026 it is Decree 220's; concluded in 2024 it is the
-- decree as made unless the parties agreed to apply Decree 220; concluded before the decree it is refused.
#ASSERT `the vintage that governs` `a contract concluded in August 2026` EQUALS `Decree 67/2023 as amended by Decree 220/2026`
#ASSERT `the vintage that governs` `a contract concluded in 2024` EQUALS `Decree 67/2023 as made`
#ASSERT `the vintage that governs` `a contract concluded in 2024 and amended to apply Decree 220` EQUALS `Decree 67/2023 as amended by Decree 220/2026`
#ASSERT REFUSED `the vintage that governs` `a contract concluded before the decree`
-- [A04.2] The two vintages name the third party differently (the strings are VN-10's; not quoted here), the same persons.
#ASSERT NOT (`the term for the third party in` `the decree as made` EQUALS `the term for the third party in` `the decree as amended`)
-- [A04.3] Through the contract: the standard third party in the 2024 contract is a third person; the driver is not; and a
-- contract concluded before the decree answers nothing.
#ASSERT `Dieu 58(1): the insurer's liability arises` (`the Law's liability claim of the third party under the contract` `a contract concluded in 2024` `a third party who was harmed` `the standard accident` FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `Dieu 58(1): the insurer's liability arises` (`the Law's liability claim of the third party under the contract` `a contract concluded in 2024` `the driver who was harmed` `the standard accident` FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT `Dieu 58(1): the insurer's liability arises` (`the Law's liability claim of the third party under the contract` `a contract concluded in 2024 and amended to apply Decree 220` `a third party who was harmed` `the standard accident` FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT REFUSED `Dieu 58(1): the insurer's liability arises` (`the Law's liability claim of the third party under the contract` `a contract concluded before the decree` `a third party who was harmed` `the standard accident` FALSE TRUE)

-- [A16.1] Art 5 owes the owner's liability to third parties AND passengers: the passenger, no third party under Art 3(5)(a),
-- is a person to whom the insured liability is owed, so a passenger's claim engages the insurer; the driver and a person on
-- the vehicle (who is not a passenger) do not; the owner who has not handed the car over does not.
#ASSERT `Dieu 58(1): the insurer's liability arises` (`the Law's liability claim of a person the owner's insured liability is owed to` `the decree as made` `a passenger on the vehicle who was harmed` `the standard accident` `a contract concluded in 2024` FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT `Dieu 58(1): the insurer's liability arises` (`the Law's liability claim of a person the owner's insured liability is owed to` `the decree as made` `a third party who was harmed` `the standard accident` `a contract concluded in 2024` FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `Dieu 58(1): the insurer's liability arises` (`the Law's liability claim of a person the owner's insured liability is owed to` `the decree as made` `the driver who was harmed` `the standard accident` `a contract concluded in 2024` FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `Dieu 58(1): the insurer's liability arises` (`the Law's liability claim of a person the owner's insured liability is owed to` `the decree as made` `a person on the vehicle who was harmed` `the standard accident` `a contract concluded in 2024` FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `Dieu 58(1): the insurer's liability arises` (`the Law's liability claim of a person the owner's insured liability is owed to` `the decree as made` `the owner of the vehicle who was harmed` `the standard accident` `a contract concluded in 2024` FALSE TRUE)
-- [A16.2] The contrast with A03: the same passenger, the same accident, the Law's engaged liability by Art 5 and not by Art 3(5)(a),
-- in both decree vintages.
#ASSERT `Dieu 58(1): the insurer's liability arises` (`the Law's liability claim of a person the owner's insured liability is owed to` `the decree as amended` `a passenger on the vehicle who was harmed` `the standard accident` `a contract concluded in 2024` FALSE TRUE) AND NOT `Dieu 58(1): the insurer's liability arises` (`the Law's liability claim of the decree's third party` `the decree as amended` `a passenger on the vehicle who was harmed` `the standard accident` `a contract concluded in 2024` FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT `Dieu 58(1): the insurer's liability arises` (`the Law's liability claim of a person the owner's insured liability is owed to` `the decree as made` `a passenger on the vehicle who was harmed` `the standard accident` `a contract concluded in 2024` FALSE TRUE) AND NOT `Dieu 58(1): the insurer's liability arises` (`the Law's liability claim of the decree's third party` `the decree as made` `a passenger on the vehicle who was harmed` `the standard accident` `a contract concluded in 2024` FALSE TRUE)
-- [A16.3] Dieu 58(1) in V1, V2 and V3 for the passenger.
#ASSERT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (YMD 2025 6 1) (`Dieu 58(1): the insurer's liability arises` (`the Law's liability claim of a person the owner's insured liability is owed to` `the decree as made` `a passenger on the vehicle who was harmed` `the standard accident` `a contract concluded in 2024` FALSE TRUE))
#ASSERT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (YMD 2026 3 1) (`Dieu 58(1): the insurer's liability arises` (`the Law's liability claim of a person the owner's insured liability is owed to` `the decree as made` `a passenger on the vehicle who was harmed` `the standard accident` `a contract concluded in 2024` FALSE TRUE))
#ASSERT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (YMD 2026 8 1) (`Dieu 58(1): the insurer's liability arises` (`the Law's liability claim of a person the owner's insured liability is owed to` `the decree as made` `a passenger on the vehicle who was harmed` `the standard accident` `a contract concluded in 2024` FALSE TRUE))

§§ `A05: the accident and the insured event (Dieu 4(27))`

-- Decree: "accident" (decree67:189, 295, 318) is the occurrence the owner must report (Art 12(1), 12(4)) and the insurer
-- must advance for even before it knows whether the cover applies (Art 12(3)(b), decree67:325-330). The decree itself uses
-- "insured event" once in the motor chapter, Art 12(7) (decree67:382), meaning the accident. The Law's insured event
-- (law08:178-181) is an objective event, agreed or provided by law, on which the insurer must pay.
-- The join reads the three limbs from the decree thus (assumed, not ruled; see SECTION-A.md section 3):
--   objective: not the intentional act of the owner, the driver or the injured person (Art 7(2)(a) names that act);
--   provided by law: the vehicle was in traffic or operating (Art 7(1), Art 3(2)-(3));
--   obliges the insurer: Article 7's answer on cover for this person is `covered`.
GIVEN v       IS A `A vintage of Decree 67/2023`
      p       IS A `A person harmed in the accident`
      a       IS AN `An accident`
      vehicle IS A `A motor vehicle`
GIVETH AN `An occurrence`
`the Law's occurrence made by the decree's accident, as it harmed` v p a vehicle MEANS
    `An occurrence` WITH
        `is an objective event` IS NOT (a's `the owner or the driver acted intentionally to cause the damage` OR p's `acted intentionally to cause the damage`)
        `was agreed by the parties or is provided by law` IS `the vehicle was in traffic or operating` a
        `obliges the insurer, branch or mutual organisation to compensate or pay under the contract when it occurs` IS `Article 7 — the answer on cover for the health and life of` v p a vehicle EQUALS `covered`

-- [A05.1] The standard accident, harming a third party, is an insured event in both decree vintages.
#ASSERT `Dieu 4(27): the occurrence is an insured event (su kien bao hiem)` (`the Law's occurrence made by the decree's accident, as it harmed` `the decree as made` `a third party who was harmed` `the standard accident` `a private car`)
#ASSERT `Dieu 4(27): the occurrence is an insured event (su kien bao hiem)` (`the Law's occurrence made by the decree's accident, as it harmed` `the decree as amended` `a third party who was harmed` `the standard accident` `a private car`)
-- [A05.2] Carve-outs of Art 7(2): the accident happened, and is the decree's accident, but is no insured event.
-- Intentional act of the owner or driver, or of the injured person; the driver fled; no licence; war; no traffic.
#ASSERT NOT `Dieu 4(27): the occurrence is an insured event (su kien bao hiem)` (`the Law's occurrence made by the decree's accident, as it harmed` `the decree as made` `a third party who was harmed` `an accident caused by an intentional act of the owner or the driver` `a private car`)
#ASSERT NOT `Dieu 4(27): the occurrence is an insured event (su kien bao hiem)` (`the Law's occurrence made by the decree's accident, as it harmed` `the decree as made` `a third party who acted intentionally to cause her own damage` `the standard accident` `a private car`)
#ASSERT NOT `Dieu 4(27): the occurrence is an insured event (su kien bao hiem)` (`the Law's occurrence made by the decree's accident, as it harmed` `the decree as made` `a third party who was harmed` `an accident in which the driver fled without performing the owner's liability` `a private car`)
#ASSERT NOT `Dieu 4(27): the occurrence is an insured event (su kien bao hiem)` (`the Law's occurrence made by the decree's accident, as it harmed` `the decree as made` `a third party who was harmed` `an accident in which the driver had no driving licence` `a private car`)
#ASSERT NOT `Dieu 4(27): the occurrence is an insured event (su kien bao hiem)` (`the Law's occurrence made by the decree's accident, as it harmed` `the decree as made` `a third party who was harmed` `an accident caused by war, terrorism or an earthquake` `a private car`)
#ASSERT NOT `Dieu 4(27): the occurrence is an insured event (su kien bao hiem)` (`the Law's occurrence made by the decree's accident, as it harmed` `the decree as made` `a third party who was harmed` `an accident of a vehicle neither in traffic nor operating` `a private car`)
-- [A05.3] The carve-out of Art 3(5)(a) bites too: the driver's own harm in the standard accident is an accident, reportable,
-- but no insured event, because the cover answers that the person is neither a third party nor a passenger.
#ASSERT `Article 7 — the answer on cover for the health and life of` `the decree as made` `the driver who was harmed` `the standard accident` `a private car` EQUALS `outside the scope: the person is neither a third party nor a passenger` AND NOT `Dieu 4(27): the occurrence is an insured event (su kien bao hiem)` (`the Law's occurrence made by the decree's accident, as it harmed` `the decree as made` `the driver who was harmed` `the standard accident` `a private car`)
-- [A05.4] A passenger's harm IS an insured event, though a passenger is no third party (Art 7(1)(b)).
#ASSERT `Dieu 4(27): the occurrence is an insured event (su kien bao hiem)` (`the Law's occurrence made by the decree's accident, as it harmed` `the decree as made` `a passenger on the vehicle who was harmed` `the standard accident` `a private car`)
-- [A05.5] The limbs split the decree's exclusions: the intentional act destroys objectivity, the Law's first limb; a flight
-- from the scene or an unlicensed driver leaves the event objective and removes only the obligation to pay (third limb).
#ASSERT NOT (`the Law's occurrence made by the decree's accident, as it harmed` `the decree as made` `a third party who was harmed` `an accident caused by an intentional act of the owner or the driver` `a private car`)'s `is an objective event`
#ASSERT (`the Law's occurrence made by the decree's accident, as it harmed` `the decree as made` `a third party who was harmed` `an accident in which the driver fled without performing the owner's liability` `a private car`)'s `is an objective event`
#ASSERT NOT (`the Law's occurrence made by the decree's accident, as it harmed` `the decree as made` `a third party who was harmed` `an accident in which the driver fled without performing the owner's liability` `a private car`)'s `obliges the insurer, branch or mutual organisation to compensate or pay under the contract when it occurs`
-- [A05.6] Dieu 4(27) in V1, V2 and V3.
#ASSERT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (YMD 2025 6 1) (`Dieu 4(27): the occurrence is an insured event (su kien bao hiem)` (`the Law's occurrence made by the decree's accident, as it harmed` `the decree as made` `a third party who was harmed` `the standard accident` `a private car`))
#ASSERT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (YMD 2026 3 1) (`Dieu 4(27): the occurrence is an insured event (su kien bao hiem)` (`the Law's occurrence made by the decree's accident, as it harmed` `the decree as made` `a third party who was harmed` `the standard accident` `a private car`))
#ASSERT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (YMD 2026 8 1) (`Dieu 4(27): the occurrence is an insured event (su kien bao hiem)` (`the Law's occurrence made by the decree's accident, as it harmed` `the decree as made` `a third party who was harmed` `the standard accident` `a private car`))

§§ `A06: the premium (Dieu 4(28)) against Annex I`

-- Decree: Annex I fixes the premium of a vehicle class for one year, VAT not included (decree67:233-234), and Art 8(2) lets
-- the insurer move it by at most 15% either way (decree67:235-238). The Law's premium (law08:182-185) is any sum the buyer must
-- pay the insurer by law or by agreement, with no band. A premium outside the decree's band is still the Law's premium.
-- Assumed, not ruled: `is required by law` is read as "the decree fixes a premium for this contract", `agreed by the parties` as "a premium
-- was paid under it" (added 2026-10-13, MIRRORBALL.md b3), and `is made by the policyholder` as "a premium was paid" (SECTION-A.md section 3).
GIVEN c IS A `A contract of compulsory motor insurance`
GIVETH AN EITHER `A problem with the facts` NUMBER
`the decree's verdict on the premium actually paid under` c MEANS
    CONSIDER `Annex I — the premium for the term of` c
    WHEN LEFT problem THEN LEFT problem
    WHEN RIGHT annex THEN `Article 8(2) — the premium after an adjustment of` ((c's `the premium paid` DIVIDED BY annex) MINUS 1) `to` annex

GIVEN c IS A `A contract of compulsory motor insurance`
GIVETH A `A payment`
`the Law's payment made for the decree's premium under` c MEANS
    `A payment` WITH
        `is made by the policyholder to the insurer, branch or mutual organisation` IS c's `the premium paid` GREATER THAN 0
        `is required by law or agreed by the parties in the contract` IS c's `the premium paid` GREATER THAN 0 OR NOT `the decree finds a problem in` (`Annex I — the premium for the term of` c)

-- [A06.1] The Annex I premium (437,000 for a private car of 5 seats, one year) paid in full is the Law's premium and the decree's lawful one.
#ASSERT `Dieu 4(28): the payment is insurance premium (phi bao hiem)` (`the Law's payment made for the decree's premium under` `a contract concluded in 2024`) AND NOT `the decree finds a problem in` (`the decree's verdict on the premium actually paid under` `a contract concluded in 2024`)
-- [A06.2] 10% above Annex I: within Art 8(2); the Law's premium too.
#ASSERT `Dieu 4(28): the payment is insurance premium (phi bao hiem)` (`the Law's payment made for the decree's premium under` `a contract of 2024 with a premium 10% above Annex I`) AND NOT `the decree finds a problem in` (`the decree's verdict on the premium actually paid under` `a contract of 2024 with a premium 10% above Annex I`)
-- [A06.3] 20% above Annex I: outside Art 8(2) (a problem with the facts), yet still the Law's premium, since the parties agreed it:
-- the Law's term is wider than the decree's lawful premium.
#ASSERT `Dieu 4(28): the payment is insurance premium (phi bao hiem)` (`the Law's payment made for the decree's premium under` `a contract of 2024 with a premium 20% above Annex I`) AND `the decree finds a problem in` (`the decree's verdict on the premium actually paid under` `a contract of 2024 with a premium 20% above Annex I`)
-- [A06.4] Carve-out: nothing paid, no premium.
#ASSERT NOT `Dieu 4(28): the payment is insurance premium (phi bao hiem)` (`the Law's payment made for the decree's premium under` `a contract of 2024 on which no premium was paid`)
-- [A06.5] Dieu 4(28) in V1, V2 and V3.
#ASSERT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (YMD 2025 6 1) (`Dieu 4(28): the payment is insurance premium (phi bao hiem)` (`the Law's payment made for the decree's premium under` `a contract concluded in 2024`))
#ASSERT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (YMD 2026 3 1) (`Dieu 4(28): the payment is insurance premium (phi bao hiem)` (`the Law's payment made for the decree's premium under` `a contract concluded in 2024`))
#ASSERT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (YMD 2026 8 1) (`Dieu 4(28): the payment is insurance premium (phi bao hiem)` (`the Law's payment made for the decree's premium under` `a contract concluded in 2024`))

§§ `A07: the limit of liability (Dieu 59) against Article 6`

-- Decree Art 6 (decree67:187-196): 150 million per person per accident for health and life; 50 or 100 million per accident for property,
-- by the kind of vehicle. Art 12(8) (decree67:386-388) pays nothing above the limit "except where the owner took voluntary insurance".
-- The Law (law08:1090-1107): the limit is the sum the insurer pays the INSURED under the contract; the total of the sum the insured owes
-- the third person, the dispute costs and the interest is capped by it unless the contract agrees otherwise (Dieu 59(4)).
-- The Law's record has ONE limit per claim and no "per person": the join builds one Law claim per person (health, life) or per accident (property).
GIVEN harm IS A `A harm a limit of Article 6 applies to`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the limit Article 6 sets for` harm MEANS
    CONSIDER harm
    WHEN `harm to the health or life of one person` THEN `Article 6(1) — the limit for health and life, per person per accident`
    WHEN `damage to property in one accident` cls THEN `Article 6(2) — the limit for property, per accident, for a vehicle of class` cls

GIVEN harm      IS A `A harm a limit of Article 6 applies to`
      owed      IS A NUMBER
      voluntary IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `A liability contract and a claim`
`the Law's liability claim under the decree's limit for` harm owed voluntary MEANS
    `A liability contract and a claim` WITH
        `a third person claimed compensation from the insured person` IS TRUE
        `the act causing the damage occurred within the insurance term` IS TRUE
        `the third person's claim was made within the insurance term` IS FALSE
        `the third person claims directly from the insurer` IS FALSE
        `the law provides that the third person may claim directly` IS FALSE
        `amount the insured person must pay the third person by law` IS owed
        `costs of resolving the dispute on liability to the third person` IS 0
        `interest payable to the third person for the insured person's late payment as the insurer directed` IS 0
        `limit of liability` IS `the limit Article 6 sets for` harm
        `the contract agrees otherwise on the limit` IS voluntary
        `the insured person must post a bond or deposit to keep the property from detention or to avoid a suit` IS FALSE
        `the insured person asks the insurer to give the bond or deposit` IS FALSE
        `the contract so agrees` IS FALSE
        `the insurer negotiates with the third person for the insured person` IS FALSE
        `the contract agrees otherwise on representation` IS FALSE

-- [A07.1] Under the limit the insurer pays what is owed; over it, the limit: the decree's number is the Law's limit of liability
-- and the Law's total agrees with Art 12(8).
#ASSERT `Dieu 59(2)-(4): the total the insurer pays` (`the Law's liability claim under the decree's limit for` `harm to the health or life of one person` 100_000_000 FALSE) EQUALS 100_000_000
#ASSERT `Dieu 59(2)-(4): the total the insurer pays` (`the Law's liability claim under the decree's limit for` `harm to the health or life of one person` 200_000_000 FALSE) EQUALS 150_000_000
#ASSERT `Dieu 59(2)-(4): the total the insurer pays` (`the Law's liability claim under the decree's limit for` `harm to the health or life of one person` 200_000_000 FALSE) EQUALS `Article 12(8) — the compensation within the limit` 200_000_000 150_000_000
-- [A07.2] Property, by the kind of vehicle: 100 million for a car, 50 million for a two-wheeled motorcycle.
#ASSERT `Dieu 59(2)-(4): the total the insurer pays` (`the Law's liability claim under the decree's limit for` (`damage to property in one accident` (`a car not used for transport business` 5)) 120_000_000 FALSE) EQUALS 100_000_000
#ASSERT `Dieu 59(2)-(4): the total the insurer pays` (`the Law's liability claim under the decree's limit for` (`damage to property in one accident` (`a two-wheeled motorcycle` 150)) 120_000_000 FALSE) EQUALS 50_000_000
-- [A07.3] Carve-out (Art 12(8), voluntary insurance): the Law lets the contract agree another limit and then gives no total; the join does not guess one.
#ASSERT REFUSED `Dieu 59(2)-(4): the total the insurer pays` (`the Law's liability claim under the decree's limit for` `harm to the health or life of one person` 200_000_000 TRUE)
-- [A07.4] The scope difference: two injured persons each owed 100 million are two decree limits (200 million paid), but one Law claim of 200 million is capped at 150 million,
-- because the Law's limit carries no "per person".
#ASSERT `Dieu 59(2)-(4): the total the insurer pays` (`the Law's liability claim under the decree's limit for` `harm to the health or life of one person` 200_000_000 FALSE) EQUALS 150_000_000 AND `Article 12(8) — the compensation within the limit` 100_000_000 150_000_000 PLUS `Article 12(8) — the compensation within the limit` 100_000_000 150_000_000 EQUALS 200_000_000
-- [A07.5] Dieu 59 in V1, V2 and V3 (no vintage arm).
#ASSERT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (YMD 2025 6 1) (`Dieu 59(2)-(4): the total the insurer pays` (`the Law's liability claim under the decree's limit for` `harm to the health or life of one person` 200_000_000 FALSE) EQUALS 150_000_000)
#ASSERT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (YMD 2026 3 1) (`Dieu 59(2)-(4): the total the insurer pays` (`the Law's liability claim under the decree's limit for` `harm to the health or life of one person` 200_000_000 FALSE) EQUALS 150_000_000)
#ASSERT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (YMD 2026 8 1) (`Dieu 59(2)-(4): the total the insurer pays` (`the Law's liability claim under the decree's limit for` `harm to the health or life of one person` 200_000_000 FALSE) EQUALS 150_000_000)

§§ `A08: compulsory insurance (Dieu 8) against the decree as a whole`

-- The Law lists four compulsory insurances; the first is the civil liability of motor vehicle owners (law08:229). The decree is the
-- Government's rule under Dieu 8(5) (law08:244-245, which VN-29 declines because "its decree is not among the sources"):
-- Art 4(2) (decree67:109-111) makes the parties use this decree's conditions, premium and minimum sums. Art 4(3) lets them agree wider cover for an
-- extra premium and obliges the insurer to separate the compulsory part (decree67:112-118). VN-10 holds that split as two Booleans, so
-- the join names the two parts. The extension is no compulsory insurance.
`a product that is compulsory motor insurance` MEANS `A product for the purposes of compulsory insurance` WITH
    `protects the public interest, the environment and social safety` IS TRUE
    `is civil liability insurance of motor vehicle owners` IS TRUE
    `is compulsory fire and explosion insurance` IS FALSE
    `is insurance in construction investment activity` IS FALSE
    `is insurance in construction activity` IS FALSE
    `is compulsory under another law and meets Dieu 8(1)` IS FALSE

`a product that is no compulsory insurance` MEANS `A product for the purposes of compulsory insurance` WITH
    `protects the public interest, the environment and social safety` IS FALSE
    `is civil liability insurance of motor vehicle owners` IS FALSE
    `is compulsory fire and explosion insurance` IS FALSE
    `is insurance in construction investment activity` IS FALSE
    `is insurance in construction activity` IS FALSE
    `is compulsory under another law and meets Dieu 8(1)` IS FALSE

GIVEN part IS A `A part of the cover`
GIVETH A `A product for the purposes of compulsory insurance`
`the Law's product that the decree's part of the cover is` part MEANS
    CONSIDER part
    WHEN `the part the decree requires`                         THEN `a product that is compulsory motor insurance`
    WHEN `an extension the parties agreed under Article 4(3)`   THEN `a product that is no compulsory insurance`

-- [A08.1] The part the decree requires is compulsory insurance under Dieu 8(2)(a), in V1, V2 and V3 (the construction limb is the one that changes).
#ASSERT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (YMD 2025 6 1) (`Dieu 8(2): the product is compulsory insurance` (`the Law's product that the decree's part of the cover is` `the part the decree requires`))
#ASSERT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (YMD 2026 3 1) (`Dieu 8(2): the product is compulsory insurance` (`the Law's product that the decree's part of the cover is` `the part the decree requires`))
#ASSERT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (YMD 2026 8 1) (`Dieu 8(2): the product is compulsory insurance` (`the Law's product that the decree's part of the cover is` `the part the decree requires`))
-- [A08.2] Carve-out (Art 4(3)): the extension the parties agree is not.
#ASSERT NOT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (YMD 2025 6 1) (`Dieu 8(2): the product is compulsory insurance` (`the Law's product that the decree's part of the cover is` `an extension the parties agreed under Article 4(3)`))
#ASSERT NOT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (YMD 2026 3 1) (`Dieu 8(2): the product is compulsory insurance` (`the Law's product that the decree's part of the cover is` `an extension the parties agreed under Article 4(3)`))
#ASSERT NOT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (YMD 2026 8 1) (`Dieu 8(2): the product is compulsory insurance` (`the Law's product that the decree's part of the cover is` `an extension the parties agreed under Article 4(3)`))
-- [A08.3] The decree enforces the split the Law's product test presupposes: an extension sold without the compulsory part separated is non-compliant.
#ASSERT NOT `Article 4(3) — the insurer has separated the compulsory part as required` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `Article 4(3) — the insurer has separated the compulsory part as required` TRUE TRUE

§§ `A09: the time to file the claim (Dieu 30), which the decree does not set`

-- The decree sets no time to file the claim file of Art 13 (decree67:401-450). Art 12(4) sets 5 working days for the NOTICE of the accident, not
-- for the claim (decree67:335-338). The Law's year (law08:707-710) therefore governs, run from the decree's own date of the accident,
-- and the decree's exception for "force majeure or an objective obstacle" (decree67:335-336) is the Law's (law08:708-710).
GIVEN a         IS AN `An accident`
      submitted IS A DATE
      fm        IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `A claim`
`the Law's claim made on the decree's accident, with the dossier submitted on` a submitted fm MEANS
    `A claim` WITH
        `date of the insured event` IS a's `date of the accident`
        `days of force majeure or objective obstacle` IS fm
        `the claimant proves they did not know when the insured event occurred` IS FALSE
        `date the insured person or beneficiary learned of the insured event` IS YMD 2000 1 1
        `a third person claimed compensation from the policyholder` IS FALSE
        `date of the third person's claim` IS YMD 2000 1 1
        `date the claim dossier was submitted` IS submitted
        `date the insurer received the full and valid dossier` IS YMD 2000 1 1
        `date the insurer paid` IS YMD 2000 1 1
        `days agreed in the contract for payment` IS NOTHING
        `amount paid late` IS 0
        `daily interest rate agreed under the Civil Code` IS NOTHING

-- [A09.1] Accident 2024-06-15: the last day is 2025-06-15; on that day the dossier is in time, the day after it is not.
#ASSERT `Dieu 30: the last day for submitting the claim dossier` (`the Law's claim made on the decree's accident, with the dossier submitted on` `the standard accident` (YMD 2025 6 15) 0) EQUALS YMD 2025 6 15
#ASSERT `Dieu 30: the dossier was submitted in time` (`the Law's claim made on the decree's accident, with the dossier submitted on` `the standard accident` (YMD 2025 6 15) 0)
#ASSERT NOT `Dieu 30: the dossier was submitted in time` (`the Law's claim made on the decree's accident, with the dossier submitted on` `the standard accident` (YMD 2025 6 16) 0)
-- [A09.2] 20 days of force majeure do not count: the day after is then in time (the decree's own 5-day notice has the same exception).
#ASSERT `Dieu 30: the dossier was submitted in time` (`the Law's claim made on the decree's accident, with the dossier submitted on` `the standard accident` (YMD 2025 7 1) 20)
-- [A09.3] Dieu 30 in V1, V2 and V3.
#ASSERT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (YMD 2025 6 1) (`Dieu 30: the dossier was submitted in time` (`the Law's claim made on the decree's accident, with the dossier submitted on` `the standard accident` (YMD 2025 6 15) 0))
#ASSERT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (YMD 2026 3 1) (`Dieu 30: the dossier was submitted in time` (`the Law's claim made on the decree's accident, with the dossier submitted on` `the standard accident` (YMD 2025 6 15) 0))
#ASSERT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (YMD 2026 8 1) (`Dieu 30: the dossier was submitted in time` (`the Law's claim made on the decree's accident, with the dossier submitted on` `the standard accident` (YMD 2025 6 15) 0))

§§ `A10: the time to pay (Dieu 31), which the decree sets only for the advance`

-- The decree's 3-working-day deadline (decree67:317-319) binds the ADVANCE on compensation for harm to health and life (Art 12(3)); it sets no
-- time for paying the compensation itself. The Law's Dieu 31(1) (law08:719-724) fills it: the time the contract agrees, or 15 days from the full
-- and valid dossier; Dieu 31(2) adds interest on late payment at a rate the parties agree. Neither the decree nor VN-10 holds a time agreed
-- or a rate, so the join leaves both NOTHING and the Law's default applies.
GIVEN a        IS AN `An accident`
      received IS A DATE
      paid     IS A DATE
      late     IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `A claim`
`the Law's claim made on the decree's accident, received and paid` a received paid late MEANS
    `A claim` WITH
        `date of the insured event` IS a's `date of the accident`
        `days of force majeure or objective obstacle` IS 0
        `the claimant proves they did not know when the insured event occurred` IS FALSE
        `date the insured person or beneficiary learned of the insured event` IS YMD 2000 1 1
        `a third person claimed compensation from the policyholder` IS FALSE
        `date of the third person's claim` IS YMD 2000 1 1
        `date the claim dossier was submitted` IS YMD 2000 1 1
        `date the insurer received the full and valid dossier` IS received
        `date the insurer paid` IS paid
        `days agreed in the contract for payment` IS NOTHING
        `amount paid late` IS late
        `daily interest rate agreed under the Civil Code` IS NOTHING

-- [A10.1] Dossier complete on 2025-02-20: the last day to pay is 2025-03-07; paid on 2025-03-05 is on time, paid on 2025-03-20 is 13 days late.
#ASSERT `Dieu 31(1): the last day for the insurer to pay` (`the Law's claim made on the decree's accident, received and paid` `the standard accident` (YMD 2025 2 20) (YMD 2025 3 5) 0) EQUALS YMD 2025 3 7
#ASSERT `Dieu 31(2): the days of delay` (`the Law's claim made on the decree's accident, received and paid` `the standard accident` (YMD 2025 2 20) (YMD 2025 3 5) 0) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `Dieu 31(2): the days of delay` (`the Law's claim made on the decree's accident, received and paid` `the standard accident` (YMD 2025 2 20) (YMD 2025 3 20) 100_000_000) EQUALS 13
-- [A10.2] Interest is owed, but neither source gives its rate: the join declines, as VN-29 does.
#ASSERT REFUSED `Dieu 31(2): the interest on the late payment` (`the Law's claim made on the decree's accident, received and paid` `the standard accident` (YMD 2025 2 20) (YMD 2025 3 20) 100_000_000)
-- [A10.3] Dieu 31(1) in V1, V2 and V3.
#ASSERT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (YMD 2025 6 1) (`Dieu 31(1): the last day for the insurer to pay` (`the Law's claim made on the decree's accident, received and paid` `the standard accident` (YMD 2025 2 20) (YMD 2025 3 5) 0) EQUALS YMD 2025 3 7)
#ASSERT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (YMD 2026 3 1) (`Dieu 31(1): the last day for the insurer to pay` (`the Law's claim made on the decree's accident, received and paid` `the standard accident` (YMD 2025 2 20) (YMD 2025 3 5) 0) EQUALS YMD 2025 3 7)
#ASSERT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (YMD 2026 8 1) (`Dieu 31(1): the last day for the insurer to pay` (`the Law's claim made on the decree's accident, received and paid` `the standard accident` (YMD 2025 2 20) (YMD 2025 3 5) 0) EQUALS YMD 2025 3 7)

§§ `A11: the premium method (Dieu 87(3)) of compulsory motor insurance, which the decree replaces by a table`

-- The decree fixes the premium by table, Annex I (decree67:233-234), so no method is registered; the Law's Dieu 87(3) (law08:1776-1782) names
-- its product line and excludes it: "motor vehicle insurance, except civil liability insurance of motor vehicle owners". Law 139/2025/QH15
-- (VN-29's V2, from 2026-01-01) moves the OTHER motor insurance from registration and approval to written notice (Dieu 87(3a)) and leaves the compulsory line
-- out. So the voluntary extension an insurer may sell beside the compulsory part (Art 4(3)) changes regime on 2026-01-01; the compulsory part never has one.
GIVEN part IS A `A part of the cover`
GIVETH A `A product line for premium rules`
`the Law's product line of the decree's part of the cover` part MEANS
    CONSIDER part
    WHEN `the part the decree requires`                       THEN `compulsory civil liability insurance of motor vehicle owners`
    WHEN `an extension the parties agreed under Article 4(3)` THEN `a voluntary motor vehicle insurance product`

GIVEN part IS A `A part of the cover`
      ra   IS A BOOLEAN
      na   IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `A premium method`
`the Law's premium method for the decree's part of the cover` part ra na MEANS
    `A premium method` WITH
        `product line` IS `the Law's product line of the decree's part of the cover` part
        `registered with the Ministry of Finance` IS ra
        `approved in writing by the Ministry of Finance` IS ra
        `notified in writing to the Ministry of Finance before it was applied or changed` IS na
        `the insurer applies the method it notified` IS na

-- [A11.1] The compulsory part has no premium-method requirement in any vintage: the Law declines to ask, whatever was registered or notified.
#ASSERT REFUSED `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (YMD 2025 6 1) (`Dieu 87(3)-(3a): the premium method meets the requirement that applies to its product line` (`the Law's premium method for the decree's part of the cover` `the part the decree requires` FALSE FALSE)) BECAUSE "the premium of compulsory civil liability insurance of motor vehicle owners is fixed under Dieu 8(5); Dieu 87(3) excludes it"
#ASSERT REFUSED `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (YMD 2026 3 1) (`Dieu 87(3)-(3a): the premium method meets the requirement that applies to its product line` (`the Law's premium method for the decree's part of the cover` `the part the decree requires` TRUE TRUE)) BECAUSE "the premium of compulsory civil liability insurance of motor vehicle owners is fixed under Dieu 8(5); Dieu 87(3) and (3a) exclude it"
#ASSERT REFUSED `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (YMD 2026 8 1) (`Dieu 87(3)-(3a): the premium method meets the requirement that applies to its product line` (`the Law's premium method for the decree's part of the cover` `the part the decree requires` FALSE FALSE)) BECAUSE "the premium of compulsory civil liability insurance of motor vehicle owners is fixed under Dieu 8(5); Dieu 87(3) and (3a) exclude it"
-- [A11.2] The extension flips on 2026-01-01: registered and approved satisfies V1 only; notified and applied satisfies V2 and V3 only.
#ASSERT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (YMD 2025 6 1) (`Dieu 87(3)-(3a): the premium method meets the requirement that applies to its product line` (`the Law's premium method for the decree's part of the cover` `an extension the parties agreed under Article 4(3)` TRUE FALSE))
#ASSERT NOT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (YMD 2026 3 1) (`Dieu 87(3)-(3a): the premium method meets the requirement that applies to its product line` (`the Law's premium method for the decree's part of the cover` `an extension the parties agreed under Article 4(3)` TRUE FALSE))
#ASSERT NOT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (YMD 2026 8 1) (`Dieu 87(3)-(3a): the premium method meets the requirement that applies to its product line` (`the Law's premium method for the decree's part of the cover` `an extension the parties agreed under Article 4(3)` TRUE FALSE))
#ASSERT NOT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (YMD 2025 6 1) (`Dieu 87(3)-(3a): the premium method meets the requirement that applies to its product line` (`the Law's premium method for the decree's part of the cover` `an extension the parties agreed under Article 4(3)` FALSE TRUE))
#ASSERT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (YMD 2026 3 1) (`Dieu 87(3)-(3a): the premium method meets the requirement that applies to its product line` (`the Law's premium method for the decree's part of the cover` `an extension the parties agreed under Article 4(3)` FALSE TRUE))
#ASSERT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (YMD 2026 8 1) (`Dieu 87(3)-(3a): the premium method meets the requirement that applies to its product line` (`the Law's premium method for the decree's part of the cover` `an extension the parties agreed under Article 4(3)` FALSE TRUE))

§§ `A12 (added): the contract of insurance (Dieu 4(16))`

-- The decree uses "contract of insurance" throughout without defining it (for example Art 4(4), decree67:122-124: one contract per vehicle).
-- The Law defines it (law08:132-137). The decree carves nothing out of that definition: it limits the term (Art 9), the number of contracts per
-- vehicle (Art 4(4), 12(9)) and refunds (Art 11), and none of those makes an agreement cease to be a contract of insurance. So the
-- assertions below hold for cases the decree restricts, to show the restriction is outside the Law's definition.
-- Assumed, not ruled: "must pay premium" is read as "the decree fixes a premium for this contract" (Annex I), not as "the premium has been paid".
GIVEN c IS A `A contract of compulsory motor insurance`
GIVETH A `A contract arrangement`
`the Law's contract arrangement made by the decree's contract` c MEANS
    `A contract arrangement` WITH
        `is an agreement between the policyholder and the insurer, branch or mutual organisation` IS TRUE
        `the policyholder must pay premium under it` IS NOT `the decree finds a problem in` (`Annex I — the premium for the term of` c)
        `the insurer, branch or mutual organisation must compensate or pay as agreed under it` IS TRUE
        `several insurers or branches of foreign non-life insurers agreed to make it with the policyholder in one contract` IS FALSE
        `they take premium and compensate or pay in the ratio agreed in the contract` IS FALSE

GIVEN c IS A `A contract of compulsory motor insurance`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the decree permits the term of` c MEANS
    `the decree answers yes in` (`Article 9 — the term is permitted for` c)

-- [A12.1] The standard contract is a contract of insurance under Dieu 4(16), in V1, V2 and V3.
#ASSERT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (YMD 2025 6 1) (`Dieu 4(16): the arrangement is a contract of insurance` (`the Law's contract arrangement made by the decree's contract` `a contract concluded in 2024`))
#ASSERT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (YMD 2026 3 1) (`Dieu 4(16): the arrangement is a contract of insurance` (`the Law's contract arrangement made by the decree's contract` `a contract concluded in 2024`))
#ASSERT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (YMD 2026 8 1) (`Dieu 4(16): the arrangement is a contract of insurance` (`the Law's contract arrangement made by the decree's contract` `a contract concluded in 2024`))
-- [A12.2] A term of four years breaches Art 9 (3 years at most) and is still a contract of insurance.
#ASSERT `Dieu 4(16): the arrangement is a contract of insurance` (`the Law's contract arrangement made by the decree's contract` `a contract of four years`) AND (NOT `the decree permits the term of` `a contract of four years`) AND `the decree permits the term of` `a contract concluded in 2024`
-- [A12.3] A second contract on the same car does not pay and is refunded in full (Art 12(9)); both are contracts of insurance.
#ASSERT `Dieu 4(16): the arrangement is a contract of insurance` (`the Law's contract arrangement made by the decree's contract` `a second contract for the same car, concluded in June 2024`) AND `Article 12(9) — what becomes of` `a second contract for the same car, concluded in June 2024` `among` (LIST `a contract concluded in 2024`, `a second contract for the same car, concluded in June 2024`) EQUALS `this contract does not pay, and its premium is refunded in full` 437000
#ASSERT `Article 12(9) — what becomes of` `a contract concluded in 2024` `among` (LIST `a contract concluded in 2024`, `a second contract for the same car, concluded in June 2024`) EQUALS `this is the contract that pays`
-- [A12.4] An unpaid premium: still a contract of insurance (the premium is due), though its payer is not yet the Law's policyholder (A01.2).
#ASSERT `Dieu 4(16): the arrangement is a contract of insurance` (`the Law's contract arrangement made by the decree's contract` `a contract of 2024 on which no premium was paid`)

§§ `A13 (added): the refusal to sell (Dieu 8(4)) against Article 4(5)(a)`

-- The decree gives the insurer a RIGHT to refuse to sell the compulsory insurance for a vehicle past its service life (Art 4(5)(a), decree67:125-128).
-- The Law forbids an authorised insurer to refuse a buyer who meets the conditions the law sets (Dieu 8(4), law08:240-243). VN-10 already notes that
-- the two agree; the join writes the bridge as code: the buyer meets the conditions only if Art 4(5)(a)'s ground is absent. That bridge is
-- an assumption (SECTION-A.md section 3): nothing in either text says the right to refuse IS a condition of buying.
GIVEN vehicle IS A `A motor vehicle`
      refused IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `A sale of compulsory insurance`
`the Law's sale of compulsory insurance of the decree's vehicle` vehicle refused MEANS
    `A sale of compulsory insurance` WITH
        `the buyer is within the class that must buy it` IS `Article 4(1) — the person must buy the compulsory motor insurance` (`Article 2(1) — the decree applies, for the motor insurance, to the person` TRUE TRUE)
        `the seller is permitted to offer it` IS TRUE
        `the buyer meets the conditions the law sets for buying` IS NOT `Article 4(5)(a) — the insurer may refuse to sell the insurance for` vehicle
        `the seller refused to sell` IS refused

-- [A13.1] An insurer who refuses a private car within its service life breaches Dieu 8(4), in V1, V2 and V3.
#ASSERT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (YMD 2025 6 1) (`Dieu 8(4): the refusal to sell breaches Dieu 8(4)` (`the Law's sale of compulsory insurance of the decree's vehicle` `a private car` TRUE))
#ASSERT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (YMD 2026 3 1) (`Dieu 8(4): the refusal to sell breaches Dieu 8(4)` (`the Law's sale of compulsory insurance of the decree's vehicle` `a private car` TRUE))
#ASSERT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (YMD 2026 8 1) (`Dieu 8(4): the refusal to sell breaches Dieu 8(4)` (`the Law's sale of compulsory insurance of the decree's vehicle` `a private car` TRUE))
-- [A13.2] Carve-out (Art 4(5)(a)): the same refusal of a car past its service life breaches nothing.
#ASSERT NOT `Dieu 8(4): the refusal to sell breaches Dieu 8(4)` (`the Law's sale of compulsory insurance of the decree's vehicle` `a private car past its service life` TRUE)
-- [A13.3] No refusal, no breach; and the buyer is bound to buy (Dieu 8(3)) through Art 4(1).
#ASSERT NOT `Dieu 8(4): the refusal to sell breaches Dieu 8(4)` (`the Law's sale of compulsory insurance of the decree's vehicle` `a private car` FALSE)
#ASSERT `Dieu 8(3): the buyer is bound to buy compulsory insurance` (`the Law's sale of compulsory insurance of the decree's vehicle` `a private car` FALSE)

§§ `A14 (added): the person paid (Art 12(5)) against the beneficiary (Dieu 4(26))`

-- Art 12(5) (decree67:341-349) pays the insured, or the injured person directly when the insured has died or lost civil capacity.
-- The Law's beneficiary (law08:175-177) is a person DESIGNATED by the buyer or the insured to receive the money. The decree designates no one: it
-- names the payee by operation of the rule. So the injured person, though paid, is no beneficiary unless a designation (a fact neither
-- the decree nor VN-10 holds) is supplied; the Law's own route to that payment is Dieu 58(2) and 61 (A03.6).
GIVEN gone       IS A BOOLEAN
      c          IS A `A contract of compulsory motor insurance`
      designated IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `A role in a contract`
`the Law's role of the person the decree has paid, designated or not` gone c designated MEANS
    CONSIDER `Article 12(5) — the insurer pays` gone
    WHEN `the insurer`                        THEN `a person with no role in the contract`
    WHEN `the injured person`                 THEN
        `A role in a contract` WITH
            `concluded the contract of insurance with an insurer, branch or mutual organisation` IS FALSE
            `pays the insurance premium` IS FALSE
            `has property, civil liability, health, life, an obligation or an economic interest insured under the contract` IS FALSE
            `was designated by the policyholder or the insured person to receive the insurance money as the contract agrees` IS designated
    WHEN `the insurance buyer or the insured` THEN
        `A role in a contract` WITH
            `concluded the contract of insurance with an insurer, branch or mutual organisation` IS TRUE
            `pays the insurance premium` IS c's `the premium paid` GREATER THAN 0
            `has property, civil liability, health, life, an obligation or an economic interest insured under the contract` IS TRUE
            `was designated by the policyholder or the insured person to receive the insurance money as the contract agrees` IS designated
    WHEN `the vehicle owner`                  THEN `a person with no role in the contract`

-- [A14.1] Insured alive: the insurer pays the buyer-or-insured, who is the insured person and no beneficiary. Insured dead: the injured person is paid and is no beneficiary.
#ASSERT NOT `Dieu 4(26): the person is a beneficiary (nguoi thu huong)` (`the Law's role of the person the decree has paid, designated or not` FALSE `a contract concluded in 2024` FALSE)
#ASSERT `Dieu 4(25): the person is the insured person (nguoi duoc bao hiem)` (`the Law's role of the person the decree has paid, designated or not` FALSE `a contract concluded in 2024` FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `Dieu 4(26): the person is a beneficiary (nguoi thu huong)` (`the Law's role of the person the decree has paid, designated or not` TRUE `a contract concluded in 2024` FALSE)
-- [A14.2] Only a designation, which the decree never mentions, makes the injured person a beneficiary.
#ASSERT `Dieu 4(26): the person is a beneficiary (nguoi thu huong)` (`the Law's role of the person the decree has paid, designated or not` TRUE `a contract concluded in 2024` TRUE)
-- [A14.3] Dieu 4(26) in V1, V2 and V3.
#ASSERT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (YMD 2025 6 1) (NOT `Dieu 4(26): the person is a beneficiary (nguoi thu huong)` (`the Law's role of the person the decree has paid, designated or not` TRUE `a contract concluded in 2024` FALSE))
#ASSERT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (YMD 2026 3 1) (NOT `Dieu 4(26): the person is a beneficiary (nguoi thu huong)` (`the Law's role of the person the decree has paid, designated or not` TRUE `a contract concluded in 2024` FALSE))
#ASSERT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (YMD 2026 8 1) (NOT `Dieu 4(26): the person is a beneficiary (nguoi thu huong)` (`the Law's role of the person the decree has paid, designated or not` TRUE `a contract concluded in 2024` FALSE))

§§ `A15 (added): the insurer (Dieu 4(17), 4(19))`

-- Art 2(4) (decree67:65-67) coins "the insurer" for the NON-LIFE insurers and the branches of foreign NON-LIFE insurers together. The Law's
-- Dieu 4(17) (law08:138-144) is the insurer of any of three kinds (life, non-life, health) and Dieu 4(19) (law08:148-151) is the branch, a
-- separate category that is not a legal person. So the decree's term is narrower on one axis (no life or health insurer) and wider on the other
-- (it takes in the branch the Law keeps apart). VN-10 has the insurer only as a party constructor; the branch is a fact the caller supplies.
`a life insurer` MEANS `An enterprise` WITH
    `established, organised and operating under this Law and other related laws` IS TRUE
    `operates to carry on insurance business, reinsurance business and ceding` IS TRUE
    `operates to carry on reinsurance business and ceding` IS FALSE
    `operates to carry on insurance brokerage activity` IS FALSE
    `carries on life insurance` IS TRUE
    `carries on non-life insurance` IS FALSE
    `carries on health insurance` IS FALSE
    `is a legal person` IS FALSE
    `is a dependent unit of a foreign insurer or reinsurer` IS FALSE
    `the foreign insurer or reinsurer guarantees and answers for all its obligations in Vietnam` IS FALSE
    `keeps independent accounts` IS FALSE
    `was founded by members or a body representing members` IS FALSE
    `operates without a profit purpose, for mutual support among members` IS FALSE
    `is voluntary, financially autonomous and answerable only within the assets formed from microinsurance` IS FALSE
    `the foreign body is a non-life insurer` IS FALSE
    `the foreign body is a reinsurer` IS FALSE

GIVEN party  IS A `A party to the claim`
      branch IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `An enterprise`
`the Law's enterprise for the decree's insurer` party branch MEANS
    CONSIDER party
    WHEN `the insurer`                        THEN IF branch THEN `a branch of a foreign non-life insurer as the decree names it` ELSE `a non-life insurer as the decree names it`
    WHEN `the insurance buyer or the insured` THEN `an enterprise of no kind`
    WHEN `the injured person`                 THEN `an enterprise of no kind`
    WHEN `the vehicle owner`                  THEN `an enterprise of no kind`

-- [A15.1] The decree's insurer that is not a branch is the Law's insurer and its non-life kind; never life or health; never the branch kind.
#ASSERT `Dieu 4(17): the enterprise is an insurer (doanh nghiep bao hiem)` (`the Law's enterprise for the decree's insurer` `the decree's insurer` FALSE) AND `Dieu 4(17): the enterprise is a non-life insurer` (`the Law's enterprise for the decree's insurer` `the decree's insurer` FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `Dieu 4(17): the enterprise is a life insurer` (`the Law's enterprise for the decree's insurer` `the decree's insurer` FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `Dieu 4(17): the enterprise is a health insurer` (`the Law's enterprise for the decree's insurer` `the decree's insurer` FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `Dieu 4(19): the enterprise is a branch of a foreign non-life insurer` (`the Law's enterprise for the decree's insurer` `the decree's insurer` FALSE)
-- [A15.2] The decree's insurer that is a branch is the Law's branch, and NOT the Law's insurer of Dieu 4(17).
#ASSERT `Dieu 4(19): the enterprise is a branch of a foreign non-life insurer` (`the Law's enterprise for the decree's insurer` `the decree's insurer` TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `Dieu 4(17): the enterprise is an insurer (doanh nghiep bao hiem)` (`the Law's enterprise for the decree's insurer` `the decree's insurer` TRUE)
-- [A15.3] Carve-outs: no other party the decree names is an insurer; and a life insurer is the Law's insurer that the decree's term never reaches.
#ASSERT NOT `Dieu 4(17): the enterprise is an insurer (doanh nghiep bao hiem)` (`the Law's enterprise for the decree's insurer` `the insurance buyer or the insured` FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `Dieu 4(17): the enterprise is an insurer (doanh nghiep bao hiem)` (`the Law's enterprise for the decree's insurer` `the injured person` FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `Dieu 4(17): the enterprise is an insurer (doanh nghiep bao hiem)` (`the Law's enterprise for the decree's insurer` `the vehicle owner` FALSE)
#ASSERT `Dieu 4(17): the enterprise is a life insurer` `a life insurer`
-- [A15.4] Dieu 4(17) in V1, V2 and V3.
#ASSERT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (YMD 2025 6 1) (`Dieu 4(17): the enterprise is an insurer (doanh nghiep bao hiem)` (`the Law's enterprise for the decree's insurer` `the decree's insurer` FALSE))
#ASSERT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (YMD 2026 3 1) (`Dieu 4(17): the enterprise is an insurer (doanh nghiep bao hiem)` (`the Law's enterprise for the decree's insurer` `the decree's insurer` FALSE))
#ASSERT `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` (YMD 2026 8 1) (`Dieu 4(17): the enterprise is an insurer (doanh nghiep bao hiem)` (`the Law's enterprise for the decree's insurer` `the decree's insurer` FALSE))
